Fingerprint stage C part 2 (negronifp=4): one raw capture. Panel HBM on through 0351's negroni_fp_hbm,
wait 2 TE frames with the new negroni_fb_te_wait (NegroniFramebuffer.cpp, tearcheck frame counter of
0259; 17 ms timed wait when negronifb_te=0), the public MCU get-image frame (20 01 00) over the
transport that answered in step 10, HBM off right after the frame and its IRQ wait (<= 100 ms: the
exposure is at the frame, the readout needs no light; review fix), then a bounded chunked read into a
kmem buffer (negronifp_img bytes, default 183456 = 364 x 252 x 2 = DELMAR_ORIGIN_BUFFER_LEN of the
public HAL header; the BB F1 00 00 read header once under one CS), stats and a verdict line.
/dev/negroni-fp (0600) returns a 32-byte header (magic NFPI, 364, 252, len, mode, wrap, proto) + the
bytes; scripts/fp/raw-to-png.py converts a pulled dump. The G7 readout command is not known [I]: the
capture proves or refutes the public command. Applies after 0352.
Details: docs/fingerprint-plan.md section 7, patches/xnu/README-fingerprint.md.

